[354.937807, "o", " or manual? If manual, how are we measuring the potential penalty? Are the\r\n\u001b[32;133Here objective thresholds, or are we relying on intuition? If automated, how reliable is the detection mechanism, and what's the false-\r\n\u001b[32;133H-positive rate? A constant stream of unnecessary reboots would be counter-productive.\r\n\nIn the final analysis, this reboot strategy is a simple way of avoiding a penalty. More information is needed about the system state \r\n\u001b[32;133H and the cause of the potential penalties to determine how efficient it is.\r\n[decision -> reboot] {}\r\n--- reboot (penalite remise a zero) ---\r"]
