[428.598149, "o", "\n[pensee du modele] [raisonnement] Okay, here's the summary of those thoughts, tailored for an expert audience, presented in the first\r\n\u001b[32;133Ht person:\r\n\n**Initial Diagnostic Attempts**\r\n\nRight, so that initial diagnostic I ran, the 'f' approach, didn't yield the expected results. Damn. Clearly, the underlying behavior \r\n\u001b[32;133H isn't being triggered in the way I had initially hypothesized. Let me shift gears – a different, more localized probe. What about exa\r\n\u001b[32;133Hamining the logarithmic scale, 'l'? Specifically, let's look at log1 through log100. It's time to test if that reveals anything about \r\n\u001b[32;133H the system's behavior. I will now run tests involving 'l'!\r\n[decision -> uart_send] {'command': 'l'}\r"]
