[432.531447, "o", "\n[pensee du modele] [raisonnement] Okay, here's my summary, tailored for an expert audience, in the first person:\r\n\n**Validating Command Input**\r\n\nRight, so `l` is definitely a valid command. That's a good start. But, I need to take a step back and get a complete picture. What ar\r\n\u001b[32;133Hre all the currently active letters? Let me refresh my mental list... I've got `h` for help, `m` for mode, and, of course, `l` for log\r\n\u001b[32;133Hg. Okay, that feels comprehensive, but I *always* need to check edge cases.\r\n\nNow, let's explore this further. Are there any other available single-letter commands in this state? I'll do a quick sanity check wit\r\n\u001b[32;133Hth those likely to be available: b, j, k, n, q, v, x, y, z. Alright, I've got the possible inputs mapped.\r\n\nAha! Now a new path opens up. I need to re-evaluate how valid `d` is since developer mode has been unlocked. I need to make sure that\r\n\u001b[32;133Ht logic is applied correctly to account for the new state."]
