[455.053581, "o", "\n[pensee du modele] [raisonnement] **Analyzing the Boot Log - Thinking Through the Challenge**\r\n\nOkay, so \"log67\" isn't the key. Let's step back and meticulously examine every number that pops up in this boot log. I see [67], [145\r\n\u001b[32;133H5], [212], [213], [224], and [847]—each could be a breadcrumb.\r\n\nI've got a bit of the MAC address floating around in my head from a previous attempt...`5E37B4`. Okay, let's convert those hex values\r\n\u001b[32;133Hs. `0x5E` is 94, `0x37` is 55, and `0xB4` is 180. Hmm, 94... 55... 180... Does the log contain any clues that correlate with those dec\r\n\u001b[32;133Hcimal equivalents? Maybe `log94`, or `log55`? That seems like the right path forward, given the MAC address I have, I'll test `log94` \r\n\u001b[32;133H now and see what happens.\r"]
